e("  { v: '9.48', t: 'Owner mode', n: [", "  { v: '9.49', t: 'The owner\\'s world', n: [\n    'Owner mode: hire a president of business operations to set prices, sign sponsors and run ticketing for you, or keep doing it yourself. Good presidents earn more; their style (revenue first, fans first, premium, cost cutter) shows.',\n    'Sponsors: seven kinds of deals (stadium club, beer, bank, airline, technology, sportsbook and, once the owners allow it, a jersey patch). Sign, pass, or ask for 15% more and risk them walking. A club you buy comes with some deals already in place.',\n    'Local TV and radio: sign with a local network, or start the club\\'s own channel (it costs money up front and pays more after a few years).',\n    'Tickets: a season-ticket discount, premium seat prices, a family section and a student section, plus a fan survey every season on value, game day and the team. The Business tab now has charts of the club\\'s value and where the money comes from and goes.',\n    'The stadium: a three-phase stadium district (plaza and restaurants, a hotel and concert hall, offices and apartments), stadium features (grass or turf, a fan plaza, a sportsbook lounge, a giant video board), international home games abroad, and rare storms or power failures that move home games and cost millions. Insurance is on by default.',\n    'The other owners: 31 owners with names and styles (big spenders, penny-pinchers, old guard, newcomers, mavericks). Votes are counted owner by owner; they remember how you voted, who did them a favor and who insulted them. Court them over dinner. New agenda items: jersey patches, private equity, more international games, and league expansion where every owner gets a share of the fees.',\n    'Awards: Coach, Executive and Owner of the Year every season.',\n    'Money and people: sell or buy back 5% of the club, bring in a private-equity fund (once the league allows it), negotiate salaries with the GM, head coach and president you hire, and decide on extensions when their contracts run out.',\n    'Owner moments: sit down with an unhappy player, watch practice, visit a hospital, throw a draft party, and induct retired greats into the Ring of Honor (four moments a season).',\n    'Legacy: a franchise history page (banners, season by season, owners, the Ring of Honor and a club museum), 14 owner achievements, and a ranking of every owner by legacy. New owners get a guided first season on the Owner\\'s suite.',\n    'Removed from Owner mode only (the other modes keep them): Pick\\'em, the friends league, calling plays and the two-minute drill in live games (owners watch), camp battles and growth goals, the rival front offices page, the league-rule settings (the owners vote on rules now), the GM tutorial, the expansion uniform-style menu (it did nothing) and the sportsbook moment (sportsbooks are a sponsor offer now). The video board moved from stadium improvements to stadium features.',\n    'Owner saves from v9.48 keep working; the new systems start the next time you play them.',\n  ] },\n" + "  { v: '9.48', t: 'Owner mode', n: [")

